5:[["$","$L10","2.6",{"topic":{"id":"2.6","title":"Collection and Preservation of Digital Evidence","minutes":16,"summary":"Collect only what is authorized, preserve what matters, and make every material action explainable.","sections":[{"title":"Prepare the scene and the method","body":["Confirm authority, scope, safety, and the evidence question before touching a device. Photograph connections and screen state where lawful and useful. Record the device clock against a trusted reference without changing it. Identify running encryption, remote wipe risks, volatile data, and business-critical services. Assign one person to maintain the scene and action log.","There is no universally correct “pull the plug” rule. Shutting down may lose memory and active connections; live acquisition may change the system and require trusted tools. A running enterprise server, an encrypted phone, and an offline laptop require different decisions. Document the selected method, expected changes, and the person who authorized the trade-off."]},{"title":"Acquire and verify a working copy","body":["For suitable offline storage, a validated hardware write blocker helps prevent writes to the source. A bit-for-bit image can capture allocated and unallocated sectors, unlike a normal file copy. Record source and destination identifiers, tool and version, settings, start and end times, errors, and acquired size. Some formats store metadata and compressed segments; understand what the chosen format preserves.","Calculate a cryptographic hash of the acquired evidence and record it. Where the format permits, distinguish the hash of the source data from the hash of an image container. Verify the working copy before examination. A source hash may be impossible to reproduce exactly after a documented live acquisition; explain that limitation instead of inventing a match."]},{"title":"Package, protect, and preserve access","body":["Use unique exhibit identifiers, tamper-evident packaging where appropriate, and controlled storage. Protect digital copies with access controls and encryption, and manage the keys separately. For phones, isolation from networks can reduce remote alteration but may affect battery and device state; follow a tested procedure and document the choice. Never place an unfamiliar device into an untested destructive mode.","Preservation letters to providers should identify the account, records, and relevant period without requesting unrelated data. Record acknowledgment and follow-up authority for disclosure. Keep originals sealed or access-controlled, examine working copies, and log any export. Preservation includes retaining context: headers, configuration, logs, and the documentation needed to interpret the content."]}],"practice":{"title":"The running encrypted laptop","scenario":"A lawfully seized laptop is logged in, disk encryption is active, and a remote-wipe capability may exist.","steps":["Record the visible state, clock, connections, and authorization.","Escalate to a qualified examiner and identify volatile-data risks.","Compare live collection and shutdown without applying a universal rule.","Document every change and prepare a custody record before transfer."],"debrief":"A proportionate, expert-supported decision is safer than a memorized shutdown command. The record must let a reviewer understand why the method was chosen."},"terms":[],"lawIds":["bnss","bsa"],"sources":["cert","nist-guide","bnss","bsa"],"labId":"acquisition","unit":2,"objectives":["Explain prepare the scene and the method and apply it to an investigation.","Explain acquire and verify a working copy and apply it to an investigation.","Explain package, protect, and preserve access and apply it to an investigation."],"question":{"id":"q-2.6","prompt":"What is the primary purpose of a hardware write blocker?","options":["To make a forensic tool run faster.","To prevent writes to the connected source device during suitable acquisition.","To prove the identity of the computer user.","To decrypt every disk automatically."],"answer":1,"explanation":"A validated write blocker helps preserve the source; it does not prove attribution or automatically solve encryption.","unit":2}}}]]
